  "id": "DrugBank_DB11800 - MONDO_7763",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Tivozanib and Nonpapillary Renal Cell Carcinoma (NPCC) through a multi-step mechanistic pathway. Tivozanib is indicated for Renal Cell Adenocarcinoma (RCA), which in turn is linked to Sirolimus and Axitinib, both of which are indicated for NPCC. This indicates that Tivozanib may exert its effects on NPCC via a pathway involving the suppression of tumor growth through the inhibition of specific signaling pathways. The presence of multiple indications pointing to Sirolimus and Axitinib suggests that Tivozanib may act through a mechanism that targets shared molecular pathways in NPCC, potentially involving the inhibition of vascular endothelial growth factor (VEGF) or other tumor-related pathways. The integration of these indications supports the hypothesis that Tivozanib could be a candidate for repurposing in NPCC, provided further mechanistic validation is conducted to confirm its direct or indirect effects on the disease.",
